Fast Sandbox: write pulled artifacts sparse

Base: opensandbox-group/fast-sandbox main at 3d804c0 (2026-10-29), the code
OpenSandbox 1.2.0 ships for these files. Apply with `git apply`.

The node agent writes every pulled artifact densely (io.Copy), so a cached
template's root filesystem occupies its full configured size and its memory
snapshot the VM's full RAM, though both are mostly zeros. Every sandbox
reflinks that rootfs, every checkpoint stages a reflink of the sandbox's, and
a restored VM maps the template's memory file: the checksum pass and the
upload of each pause then read gigabytes of zeros from disk, and the memory
dump faults untouched guest pages in from it. copySparse skips all-zero
64 KiB runs (holes) and sets the final size with a truncate; content and
digest are unchanged, and SHA256File already hashes holes without reading.
See docs/research/fast-sandbox-pause-time.md in different-ai/differently.

